Knit your own refs: the locker owner builds the map, no bot reads the server

Plan (merge qualifies when every box holds):
- [ ] harvest shape: what any harvester emits, the owner's messages only
- [ ] js/knit.js: harvest -> refs, a map of message pointers, not a copy
  - [ ] forum post = unit; thread name = title
  - [ ] sources = every media hit; several services = listener's choice
  - [ ] lyrics = contiguous text-only posts; split lyrics -> unmatched
  - [ ] control post `locker: …` overrides; the fail-safe for everything
  - [ ] suppress: a forum or thread never lands in refs
  - [ ] unmatched list: the owner's work queue, each with the post to write
- [ ] render: refs + current harvest -> markdown (edits flow, refs don't move)
- [ ] fetch: own attachments pulled while their URLs are fresh
- [ ] harvesters: legacy bot refs.json, Discord data package
- [ ] tests against the committed real data
- [ ] IPFS out
- [ ] README: why there is no bot
